 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? The sweet spot is usually in the middle of the site, so it' not shaded by trees or rocks. Look for an open spot with good drainage. That can be tempting, but trees and tents don' mix well. A tall tree can shade the tent in the day and catch the wind you need to breathe. That's probably your best bet. Cut it off at the base with hampers or poles in place, and stake the branches down with cords. Avoid that spot. The ground around a fire is usually packed down, so a tent there tends to sink into the loose soil. Exactly. A flat, open spot is your best bet for a relaxed night's sleep.",
